The pitch of all sufficiently sustained tones can thus be determined mechanically. We find two forks, whose pitch is known, with each of which the new tone beats more slowly than the forks beat with each other, and we verify the count, by seeing that the sum of the @@R@@
>>>
<<<
@@R@@
===
beats with both forks is the number of beats of the forks with one another. The pitch number is then that of the lower fork increased by the number of beats made with it in a second, and that of the upper fork diminished by the number of beats made with it in a second. @@R@@
>>>
<<<
